Z||000005||Ozzy||09-25-2000||11:05 AM||||Thnx guys...<P>Stimpy, right now I'm not too sure other than somewhere between Sunnyvale and San luis Obispo! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I have to get back there and see what I can rent/buy for a reasonable price and I'm not tied to a commute so things are flexable. <P>It will be awhile before I get settled out there again. Seems like all I've done here is move for the last year! But, I am looking forward to Fiero-ing in California.<P><P>------------------<BR>There are 3 types of people in this world;<P><I>Those who make things happen,<BR>Those who watch things happen,<BR>And those who wonder <B>What Da hell Happened?!</B></I> <P>:D:D  Ozzy  :D:D||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||09-25-2000||11:10 AM||||I was in Sacramento yesterday.  I'm  up there a lot, but I live down in Marina CA.  I was up checking Goerge's place out last night.  My toy needs some help (86GT).  Sounds like plenty of Fiero folks are around to make you feel at home. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000007||Robert||09-25-2000||02:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ozzy:<BR><B> somewhere between Sunnyvale and San luis Obispo!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ozzy;<BR>You’re talking about a lot of space between those two cities; it’s about a 3-hour ride from San Francisco to San Luis Obispo, and about a 300% drop in rent.  San Luis Obispo is a college town; rent and food are cheep, probity the wages too.  San Francisco (and the Bay Area) has just earned the honor of MOST EXPENSIVE place to live in the US. The report said it takes a $28 per hour income to afford a medium priced apartment in San Francisco. That was one of the reasons I moved to the East Bay in the 70’s, even though I was born in San Francisco. (The other reason is I just got tired of the FOG!!!)<P>Pennock members are always welcome. Keep in touch.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||mshill||09-25-2000||06:00 PM||||Robert, you don't commute across the Bay Bridge do you?  If so, that must be a real pain in the backside (wallet included).<P>I got out of the South Bay Area (born and raised in the Cupertino/West San Jose area)<BR>about 10 years ago.  Visiting San Francisco and the east bay is great, but goin to the inlaws in the south bay is really bad.  My wife is bugging me to move on up the hill (east) a little farther to Auburn, but I like being only a few minutes from work.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ozzy||09-25-2000||08:12 PM||||Dig it...<P>Believe me I know the rent is high in the Bay area. I've been falling to the floor clutching my chest as I look on the web at rental and purchase prices.We were living up in Placerville before we left CA. and it was pretty reasonable but for the commute.<P>The awesome thing about my new gig is I'm not tied to a commute. Says right on my offer letter..."Work from Home"! The only thing that makes the sth of SJ relevant is the extra money I get for what they call a geographical allowance. Its a chunk o' change and I'm not in a hurry to give it up! I could be rapidly restoring ol' blue with the extra money if I can find something reasonable a little further south.||||reg||10
Z||000010||Big O||09-26-2000||01:02 AM||||If you're going to be in the Modesto area stop and see me at the store.  It's at 1901 D Prescott Road in Modesto.  We are always open to Fierophiles.  We just reworked the suspension on Dan Mayes 86 GT.  New shocks, struts, a tie rod end and 4 wheel alignment.  Now it goes straight down the road.||||reg||6
